2. Loans Analysis Page
Overview & Purpose
Analyzes loan portfolio health, profitability margins, monthly installment performance, distribution across customer segments, and default rates.

Key Insights
Portfolio Scale & Profitability: Generated 34.53M in Loan Profit from 600 Total Active/Closed Loans, with a Total Loan Amount of 237M and 3.96M in Total Monthly Installments.

Loan Type Breakdown: Car Loans drive the largest share of monthly installment returns (1.62M / 40.95%), followed by Personal Loans (1.31M / 33.14%) and Mortgage Loans (1.03M / 25.91%).

Segment Target Concentration: Loan issuance volume is heavily concentrated in the Retail segment (over 300 loans), outperforming the Mass segment (~180 loans), while the VIP segment accounts for the lowest loan count.

Loan Status & Portfolio Risk: The vast majority of total loan amount resides in Active status, with closed loans forming the second largest share. Defaulted loans remain minimal, reflecting disciplined credit risk management.

Seasonality in Monthly Installments: Installment collections show clear seasonal peaks during May and October (surpassing 400K), while experiencing dips in April (~200K) and December.
